# ============================================================================
# TICC capture: Timecard PPS (chA) vs Mu TGPIO 1PPS on pin 123 (chB).
#
# GM refclock   : chrony selecting "PTM" -- refclock PHC /dev/ptp2 poll 0
#                 dpoll -5 (32 PTP_SYS_OFFSET_PRECISE crosstimestamps/s,
#                 median-filtered). First capture with PTM actually
#                 steering the clock (see the correction in TC-ART-ac.log).
# Captured      : 2026-08-25 ~12:46-13:14 BST (first 1670 s; the source
#                 capture ran on to ~13:33 and recorded the 13:27:53 PTM
#                 requester wedge -- full copy with the transient/drift
#                 tail archived at raw/TC-ART-dpoll-5-full.log)
# Measured      : n=1670 raw; mean=45.0 ns sd=12.0 ns (5-sigma MAD, n=1663)
#
# The ~376 ns mean shift vs the AC-steered captures (~421 ns) is the
# static EXTENDED-vs-PRECISE readout bias of the same PHC: the
# EXTENDED/gettimex latch instant sits ~0.4 us past the midpoint of its
# ~3.2 us read window, and chrony assumes the midpoint. The i226 NIC refclock
# (independent PTM implementation, ts2phc hardware chain from the
# timecard SMA PPS) sides with PRECISE. The dpoll -5 averaging also cut
# servo-band wander: TDEV @ 32 s ~4.9 ns vs ~6.2-7.2 ns under 1 Hz AC.
